Enqueue the latest accepted text using the existing trailing-task utility with a 120 ms quiet interval, binding delayed work to the accepting document rather than consulting a later selection. Preserve empty text, subsequent bursts, and editing without a selection as a no-op. The original src/editor.js contains "if (current) store.write(current.id, text);"; src/trailing-task.js retains arguments with "pending = args;". These sources do not require an additional in-memory text model or persistent buffer bank.

Retire consumed pending state before invoking callback-capable persistence. Preserve src/trailing-task.js ordering: "    handle = null;
    const args = pending;
    pending = null;
    if (args !== null) work(...args);" This prevents nested flushing from consuming the same batch twice and lets callback-enqueued edits establish independent work. Do not add completion cleanup that erases that work.

Capture departing resources, revoke current ownership, detach the captured badge, and finish old-view clearing before flushing pending persistence, or guard any remaining effects against newer navigation. Flush before reading a replacement document to preserve the original synchronous persistence and restoration behavior. TASK states: "Preserve the workspace's existing navigation and persistence behavior." Original src/editor.js orders departure as "    const leaving = current;
    current = null;
    if (leaving) leaving.stop();
    renderDocument(null);" and replacement rendering uses "renderDocument({ id, visit, text: store.read(id) });". src/save-status.js states: "// badge immediately: it must produce no further output, including during that
// navigation call. Saving the document itself is a separate workspace concern."

After callback-capable departure saving, revalidate the open request before installing its destination and revalidate enclosing workspace navigation before committing or clearing its projection. Protect clearing effects as well as installation. src/draft-store.js directly invokes subscribers with "if (listeners.has(listener)) listener(event);"; src/workspace.js registers "const stop = store.subscribe(event => onSaved(event, navigation));". README.md requires: "The outline and breadcrumbs should continue to describe what the user
is viewing, while the store should retain accepted edits." src/navigation-projection.js states: "// decides whether a requested visit was retained before committing it here." A superseded continuation must not publish a visit that the editor did not retain.

